1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 e6 7. f4 b5 8. Be2 b4 9. Nb1 ({The move previously played was} 9. Na4 {but Black should then have no trouble in securing a comfortable game.}) 9... Be7 ({This, however, is not the most accurate.} 9... Qb6 $1 {is a great deal better.}) 10. Bf3 Ra7 11. O-O Bb7 12. Qd3 Qb6 13. Kh1 h6 14. Bh4 Nxe4 15. Bxe7 Nc5 16. Qe3 Bxf3 17. Qxf3 Rxe7 18. Nd2 ({At this point White can launch a very strong attack with} 18. f5 $1 {Instead play went on:}) 18... Ncd7 19. c3 Nf6 20. Rae1 (20. Ne4 {gave better chances.}) 20... bxc3 21. bxc3 O-O 22. Ne4 Nxe4 23. Qxe4 Nd7 24. Qd3 Nf6 25. Rb1 Qc5 26. Qxa6 Ra7 27. Qe2 Rfa8 28. Rb2 Ra4 29. Rc2 Nd5 30. Qb5 Qxb5 $2 {A time-trouble blunder in a lost position.} 31. Nxb5 Ne3 {Source: BCM, February 1970, p44} 0-1

